  "statement": "Find a formula for the sum $1\\cdot2+2\\cdot3+3\\cdot4+\\cdots+n(n+1)$.",
  "solution": "The sum is $\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r(r+1)=\\sum_{r=1}^{n}(r^{2}+r)=\\tfrac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}+\\tfrac{n(n+1)}{2}=\\tfrac{n(n+1)}{2}\\bigl(\\tfrac{2n+1}{3}+1\\bigr)=\\tfrac{n(n+1)(n+2)}{3}$.",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
